[1]`; the `0.5` accounts for the leverage term only\n","  applying to roughly half of observations (negative shocks), under a symmetric-shock assumption.\n","- **EGARCH:** `beta[1]`; the model operates on log-variance, so `beta[1]` is the direct AR(1)\n","  coefficient on lagged log-variance."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":35,"id":"4b367ab1","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.032265Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.031577Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.037174Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.03619Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.037792,"end_time":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.039727+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.001935+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def get_persistence(model_result, vol_model):\n","    \"\"\"Compute volatility persistence for a fitted GARCH-family model.\"\"\"\n","    params = model_result.params\n","    if vol_model == \"GARCH\":\n","        return params[\"alpha[1]\"] + params[\"beta[1]\"]\n","    elif vol_model == \"GJR-GARCH\":\n","        return params[\"alpha[1]\"] + params[\"beta[1]\"] + 0.5 * params[\"gamma[1]\"]\n","    elif vol_model == \"EGARCH\":\n","        return params[\"beta[1]\"]"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c5e85ebe","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.029391,"end_time":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.095454+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.066063+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Model Comparison Table**: One row per (asset, specification): AIC, BIC, log-likelihood, and persistence."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":36,"id":"97aaecd4","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.153178Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.152425Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.179686Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.17876Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.058536,"end_time":"2026-10-02T15:02:49.182+00:00","exception":false,"start_t